      "sha256": "8d860e451f20f38865b725b42d82feb714c725373dd8f3b32b8652b3eeb070ca",
      "sections": [
        "608.2f",
        "700.1",
        "601.2d",
        "603.3d"
      ],
      "scope": "Call simultaneity is a reasoned inference from general resolution/event rules; Ureni division is fixed when targets and shares are announced."
    }
  ],
  "rules_inference": {
    "Call_simultaneity": "The printed single instruction acts on several objects. All applicable choices are made before one simultaneous placement batch, aggregating repeated recipients. This follows the general 608.2f multiple-object resolution rule and 700.1 event semantics. No card-specific contrary official note was found. Pinned XMage loops addCounters sequentially; that implementation is not used as authority to split this event. Parent accepted this design pending independent rules review.",
    "proof": "One five-color Dragon receives five counters; controlled-recipient observer triggers once and batch observer triggers once. Five distinct successful recipients win; doubling one recipient does not. Prohibition clears a recipient before receipts and prevents a win."
  },
  "owned_state_and_legality": [
    "Private search and optional hand candidates remain actor-private; stale cards, wrong owner/controller, duplicate roles, wrong actors and invalid choices reject transactionally.",
    "Partial public color choices, queued counter replacement choices, optional free casts, private searches and wide division amounts are cloned after parent disposal and compared through raw/index actions and restore.",
    "CounterCompletion reuses one owned replacement batch continuation, records actual positive exact recipients before trigger dispatch, and counts distinct refs rather than counters.",
    "Color sequence vectors are bounded by five roles; reachable search states use one 32-bit mask. New rare packet/resolution allocations are included in owned-byte accounting. Normal empty data stays absent."
  ],
  "wire_and_layout_changes": [
    "New public Action::ChooseColorCounter{object}, EffectChoiceKind::ColorCounter metadata and HandChoiceKind::DiscardNonlandReflexive metadata for new choice domains.",
    "AllocateTargetAmount.amount, TargetAllocation.amount and TargetAmountChoiceView amount bounds widen losslessly from u32 to u64. Prior small serialized numeric values remain equal; raw action serde roundtrip covers greater than u32 values.",
    "SpellView.announced_division is Option<Box<u64>>, omitted when None and initializedNone in every ordinary packet constructor; copied packets retain it. It adds one rare pointer slot per stack packet, not per permanent.",
    "SearchChoiceView.distinct_colors omits zero; CascadeView.keep_exiled omits false. Existing generic search and cascade/discover values remain unchanged.",
    "Resolution.color_sequence is private optional boxed owned state; all inherited literal constructors explicitly initialize None. CounterCompletion broadens the existing boxed completion enum without an additional CounterBatch pointer.",
    "Root owns common observation schema and inherited trace acceptance; this checkpoint deliberately does not bump shared schema independently."
  ],
